> ⚠️ **GOVERNED — this PR stays a draft until an authorized approval is on it.** `node scripts/check-governed-queue-guard.mjs --test` over this PR's file list answers `GOVERNED — 1 of 42 path(s)`: `skills/objectui/guides/plugin-development.md`, the published skills catalog. One governed path governs the whole PR. ⛔ Not to be flipped ready, enqueued or armed with auto-merge until `os-zhuang` or `hotlong` leaves an APPROVED review; ⛔ no seat approves it. After that approval the claiming seat lands it.

Moves `lucide-react` from `^1.31.0` to `^1.43.0` across the workspace, repairs what the jump breaks, and executes the maintainer's **ruling C** on this PR (comment `5750512894`, verbatim 「8941 C」): relax the two pins, land the bump. The re-measured census comes first, then ruling C, then the checks. The sections under **Historical** further down were measured on older trees and are ⛔ not re-derived.

objectui#7058 (the Dependabot branch this PR superseded) is already closed, unmerged, since 2026-09-13. This PR never named it with a closing keyword; closing it was never this PR's.

## 1. This round's census — re-measured on 2026-09-25 against the INSTALLED 1.43.0

Tree: this branch after merging `main` at `21d34d5e2` (merge commit `423a1a59a`); the censuses read the committed tree through `git ls-tree` plus `git cat-file`, so enumeration and reading come from the same source. The installed `lucide-react` is 1.43.0, integrity-equal to the registry tarball (`sha512-ubtnda1f…`).

⚠️ **Correction to the baseline.** `main` does not install 1.31.0. Its manifests say `^1.31.0`, but since the `pnpm dedupe` of #9316 (2026-09-13) its lockfile resolves **1.35.0**, one copy. So this PR moves the declared range `^1.31.0` to `^1.43.0` and the installed version 1.35.0 to 1.43.0. Every comparison below is taken against both 1.31.0 and 1.35.0.

### 1a. What lucide itself changed (read off the three installed artifacts)

| Surface | 1.31.0 | 1.35.0 (main today) | 1.43.0 | Removed, 1.35.0 to 1.43.0 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| runtime exports of `lucide-react` | 6068 | 6110 | 6224 | **0** |
| public names in `lucide-react.d.ts` | 6072 | 6114 | 6230 | **0** |
| `dynamicIconImports` keys (= `iconNames`) | 2025 | 2039 | 2077 | **0** |
| keys of the runtime `icons` record | 1767 | 1781 | 1818 | **1 — `Trash2`** |
| icon modules exporting `__iconNode` | 1767 | 1781 | **0** | — |
| icon modules exporting `__iconData` | 0 | 0 | 1818 | — |
| icon modules declaring `aliases` | 0 | 0 | 248 | — |

1.31.0 to 1.43.0 also removes 0 exports, 0 type names, 0 dynamic names and the same single record key.

### 1b. Census 1 — every name this tree imports from `lucide-react` resolves

TypeScript-AST scan of every tracked code file: import and export-from declarations (named, default, namespace, `type`), `import()` / `vi.mock()` / `require.resolve()` calls naming the package, `import type` nodes, and static member reads off a namespace import or off `icons`.

| Tree | importing files | sites | distinct value names | type names | fail on 1.43.0 | fail on 1.35.0 | fail on 1.31.0 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| this branch after the merge | 413 | 1980 | 329 | 2 (`LucideIcon`, `LucideProps`) | **0** | 0 | 0 |
| `6f20cfb06` (the 2026-09-20 head) | 419 | 2018 | 331 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 0 |

Controls, in the same run: an injected `Trash`, `type LucideIcon` and namespace read `L.Pencil` resolve; an injected `NotARealLucideIcon` and `L.AlsoNotReal` are both reported as failures.

### 1c. Census 2 — every authored icon STRING resolves as a key of the runtime `icons` record

Every string in an icon-named position (`icon`, `iconName`, `...Icon` properties, JSX attributes, `resolveIcon(...)` arguments) across code, JSON, YAML and Markdown, tokenised with the seam's own rule copied verbatim (`split(/[-_\s]+/)`, capitalise, `Home` to `House`), judged against each version's record.

| Reading | Result |
|---|---|
| sites / distinct names | 717 / 207 |
| live on 1.43.0 | 641 |
| live on 1.35.0 or 1.31.0 but **dead on 1.43.0** (what the bump breaks) | **0** outside this PR's own changeset prose, which names `trash-2` as the spelling it retired |
| dead on all three versions | 75 sites, 40 distinct — pre-existing and untouched by the bump: the deliberate retired-spelling negatives (`edit`, `smile`, `filter`, `not-a-real-icon`, `definitely-not-a-lucide-icon`…) and strings that are not icon names at all (colour classes, labels) |
| `pnpm check:icon-record-names` | `OK  lucide icon names: 184 authored/declared names reaching 1 record-reading resolver are live icons keys (record 1818 keys ...)` |

Controls: an injected `icon: 'trash'` reads live, injected `icon: 'trash-2'` in JSON and in TS both read as regressions. Independently, a case-insensitive `git grep` for every spelling that tokenises to `Trash2` finds only component imports of `Trash2` (still a runtime export in 1.43.0), comments, and one `vi.mock` stub key: no authored string. The same census over `main` finds exactly 6 string sites that tokenise to `Trash2` (5 `trash-2`, 1 `Trash2`, one per file); they are the ones the 2026-09-20 round repaired, and all 6 read `trash` here.

**The glyph is unchanged by that repair**, measured on icon nodes:

| Comparison | full node | node without `key` |
|---|---|---|
| 1.43.0 `trash` vs 1.31.0 `trash-2` | IDENTICAL | IDENTICAL |
| 1.43.0 `trash` vs 1.35.0 `trash-2` | IDENTICAL | IDENTICAL |
| control: 1.43.0 `pencil` vs 1.31.0 / 1.35.0 `pencil` | IDENTICAL | IDENTICAL |
| control: 1.43.0 `trash` vs 1.35.0 `trash` | DIFFERENT | DIFFERENT |

⚠️ The last control row is also a user-visible fact: lucide moved the two-line bin artwork under the `trash` name, so anything that already authored `trash` (10 string sites on `main`) now draws what `trash-2` drew. Upstream also redrew other glyphs. Comparing the artwork each name draws on 1.35.0 against 1.43.0 (controls: `Trash2` reads unchanged, `Trash` reads changed), the ones this tree uses are the components `CheckCircle2` (29 importing files), `Table2` (8), `CircleDot` (5), `CircleCheck` (2), `Asterisk` (1) and `BadgeCheck` (1), and the strings `trash`, `shopping-cart`, `circle-check` / `CircleCheck` and `table-2`. Redraws, not breakage.

### 1d. Census 3 — every reader of `__iconNode` / `__iconData` works

A `git grep` for `__iconNode|__iconData|createLucideIcon|LucideIconData` over the whole tree finds exactly **one reader**: the lazy draw in `packages/components/src/renderers/action/resolve-icon.ts`, which reads `module.__iconData?.node ?? module.__iconNode` (the 2026-09-20 repair). No other code reads an icon module's exports. Red, then green, on the lazy-draw row, predicted red before running, through `scripts/ablation-replace.mjs` from `../objectstack` (anchor must hit exactly once, write verified on disk, restore proven by blob hash and an empty `git diff HEAD`):

```
mutation   const node = module.__iconData?.node ?? module.__iconNode;   ->   const node = module.__iconNode;
           ok mutation landed: anchor 1 -> 0, blob cc7d80e9edfc -> 271d15e3fa58
RED        x fills the path data in once the icon module arrives
           AssertionError: expected 0 to be greater than 0      Tests  1 failed | 5 skipped (6)
restore    ok restored: blob == HEAD (cc7d80e9edfc) and `git diff HEAD` is empty
GREEN      Tests  1 passed | 5 skipped (6)                       (at 423a1a59a)
```

**Real-build probe**, on the console built at `989330df0` (`apps/console/dist`), in Chromium: of 2345 built JS chunks, 1819 mention `__iconData` (the 1818 `vendor-icon-*` chunks plus the seam's `ui-components` chunk) and exactly 1 mentions `__iconNode`, the seam's fallback read; the built seam reads `__iconData?.node??n.__iconNode`. Four built icon chunks imported in the browser:

| chunk | `__iconData.name` | aliases | path elements | first `d` | `__iconNode` |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `vendor-icon-house-*` | `house` | `home` | 2 | `M15 21v-8a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-4a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v8` | undefined |
| `vendor-icon-trash-*` | `trash` | `trash-2` | 5 | `M10 11v6` | undefined |
| `vendor-icon-arrow-down-0-1-*` | `arrow-down-0-1` | `arrow-down-01` | 5 | `m3 16 4 4 4-4` | undefined |
| `vendor-icon-loader-circle-*` | `loader-circle` | `loader-2` | 1 | `M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-6.219-8.56` | undefined |

So the shipped glyph data is non-empty and sits where the seam now reads it, and the pre-repair read would find nothing in the real build too. NOT MEASURED: a rendered page. With no backend the built console lands on `/login`, which draws no lucide svg at all (0 found), so there was no seam-drawn glyph on screen to count.

### 1e. Census 4 — every `lucide-NAME` class token in the tree, against the 1.43.0 alias index

Every `lucide-` token in every tracked text file (lockfile and binaries excluded), classified against an alias index built from the 1818 installed icon modules (canonical `lucide-` plus the icon name; one alias class per declared alias), against what the seam emits (the key-derived class and the canonical class, rule copied verbatim from `lucideClassNames`), and against what 1.35.0 emitted.

| Class of token | distinct | disposition |
|---|---|---|
| canonical class of a 1.43.0 icon | 29 | safe: lucide's component and the seam both emit it |
| not an icon class (`lucide-icon`, script names such as `lucide-record-icon-names`) | 5 | out of scope |
| **alias** class: `lucide-home` (of `house`) | 1 | the button pin — relaxed under ruling C, see section 2 |
| **alias** class: `lucide-loader-2` (of `loader-circle`) | 1 | `svg-host-dom-leak-5632.test.tsx`, a spinner drawn by a component import, so lucide's own alias class IS on it; the exact assertion the 2026-09-20 round updated holds on 1.43.0 |
| **alias** / retired: `lucide-trash-2`, `lucide-trash2` | 2 | prose only: the seam docblock and the pin comment (both rewritten in this round), and the pending objectui#9251 changeset (left alone; this PR's changeset dates its example) |
| seam-key-only class (emitted by the seam, not by lucide 1.43.0) | **0** referenced | — |

Controls: an injected `svg.lucide-trash-2` assertion is classified as an alias of `trash`; an injected `svg.lucide-check` reads canonical. Six dynamically built selectors (`svg.lucide-${name}` in the command and context-menu suites) iterate canonical names only.

### 1f. New since the 2026-09-20 round

`main` moved 294 commits past the old merge base `078f2e4f7`. What the four censuses see that the `6f20cfb06` tree did not:

| Census | new at this head | verdict on 1.43.0 |
|---|---|---|
| imports | 7 sites in 6 files; 4 files import lucide for the first time: `packages/app-shell/src/layout/ReadRateBanner.tsx` (`TriangleAlert`), `packages/app-shell/src/views/ActionParamDialog.tsx` (`ChevronDown`, `Lock`), `packages/plugin-detail/src/__tests__/detailSectionAuthoredIcon-9529.test.tsx` (`MapPin`), `packages/app-shell/src/hooks/__tests__/userLocale-10059.test.tsx` (a `vi.mock` of the package); plus `Code2` in `FlowKeyValueField.tsx` and `BookOpen` in `NavigationDesigner.tsx` | all resolve |
| authored strings | 13 sites; new names `share`, `map-pin` | all live, except 2 `edit` sites in `menubar-item-icon.test.tsx`, which are deliberate retired-spelling negatives, dead on all three versions |
| `__iconNode` / `__iconData` readers | none | — |
| class tokens | 6 pairs, all in `packages/components/src/__tests__/menubar-item-icon.test.tsx`: `lucide-chevron-right`, `lucide-download`, `lucide-file`, `lucide-mail`, `lucide-save`, `lucide-share` | all canonical |

None of them needed a repair.

### 1g. The merge and the lockfile

`origin/main` **merged** at `21d34d5e2` (⛔ no rebase, no amend, no force-push): one conflict, `packages/plugin-kanban/package.json`, resolved as the union (main deleted `@tanstack/react-virtual` with the module that used it; this branch bumps `lucide-react`). `pnpm-lock.yaml` was regenerated by pnpm from main's own lockfile, ⛔ not hand-merged: main's file taken whole, then `pnpm install --lockfile-only` with the 22 manifests briefly at an exact `1.43.0` and again with `^1.43.0` restored, which pnpm keeps. A plain re-lock follows the caret to the newest 1.x (1.48.0 today). The delta against main is lucide alone: 22 importer specifiers, 22 resolutions and the fumadocs peer suffixes. All 22 manifests that declare `lucide-react` read `^1.43.0`.

## 2. Ruling C — the two pins, relaxed and no more

⚠️ **This weakens a gate that was telling the truth.** The two rows below were red because the seam genuinely stopped reproducing lucide's classes; they were not flakes. lucide-react 1.43.0 emits one class per DECLARED ALIAS (`house` renders `lucide-house lucide-home`) and no longer the class it derived from the PascalCase key. The alias list lives only inside each icon module, which objectui#9251 made lazy, while the seam must put its classes on the first frame. The maintainer chose C over A (put every alias into the eager, build-generated name list, spending bytes under objectui#9251's ruling) and over B (hold at 1.31.0), with the weakening stated when it was presented. ⇒ After this PR, a seam-drawn glyph missing lucide's alias classes, or carrying the key-derived class lucide no longer emits, passes these rows. ⛔ It is not free.

**Re-measured size of what is given up** (1.43.0 facts, the seam's rule copied verbatim): of 1818 record keys, the seam's class set and lucide's **agree on 1494 and disagree on 324** (80 seam-only, 223 lucide-only, 21 both ways) — the same figures the 2026-09-20 round read. **Why the canonical form of C and not the subset form:** the seam's classes are a subset of lucide's for only 1717 of 1818 keys (the key-derived class is not one lucide 1.43.0 emits), so "the seam's classes need only be a subset" would still be red on 101 keys. The canonical class is on the seam for **1818 of 1818**.

**Exactly two pins.** They are the two rows `Test (shard 3/4)` and `Test (shard 4/4)` reported red on `6f20cfb06`, read off those check runs' own annotations:

- shard 3/4: `button-shared-icon-resolver.test.tsx` > `resolves home through the RENAME alias to House, not to a dead home` — `expected null to be SVGSVGElement`;
- shard 4/4: `resolve-icon-lazy-9251.test.tsx` > `reproduces lucide's per-icon class names over the WHOLE record vocabulary` — `AArrowDown: expected "lucide lucide-a-arrow-down", got "lucide lucide-a-arrow-down lucide-aarrow-down"`, and nine more.

Each now carries, at its site, what it used to refuse and why it no longer does. Verbatim below, with two deliberate substitutions: the generic in `Record OF string, React.ElementType` and the placeholder in `lucide-ICONNAME` are written in capitals instead of angle brackets, because GitHub deletes tag-shaped fragments from a body even inside a code fence. Byte-exact text: `git show 178da2eea`.

### Pin 1 — `packages/components/src/renderers/action/__tests__/resolve-icon-lazy-9251.test.tsx`

Before (`6f20cfb06`):

```ts
  it('reproduces lucide\'s per-icon class names over the WHOLE record vocabulary', () => {
    // ⚠️ The class names are the part a conversion rule gets wrong silently: 95
    // of the record's keys pack digits that lucide splits in the module name and
    // not in the class derived from the key, so `Trash2` renders BOTH
    // `lucide-trash2` and `lucide-trash-2`. `createLucideIcon` is what builds
    // them and the seam no longer calls it, so every name is compared against
    // the record's own component here — not a sample, and not a copy of the
    // rule.
    const keys = Object.keys(icons);
    expect(keys.length).toBeGreaterThan(1000);
    const mismatches: string[] = [];
    let digitKeysChecked = 0;
    for (const key of keys) {
      if (/\d/.test(key)) digitKeysChecked += 1;
      const reference = renderIcon((icons as Record OF string, React.ElementType)[key], {});
      const seam = renderIcon(resolveIcon(key)!, {});
      const want = classesOf(reference).join(' ');
      const got = classesOf(seam).join(' ');
      if (want !== got) mismatches.push(`${key}: expected "${want}", got "${got}"`);
    }
    expect(mismatches.slice(0, 10)).toEqual([]);
    // Non-vacuity, both ways: the loop ran, and it ran over the class of name
    // this row exists for.
    expect(digitKeysChecked).toBeGreaterThan(50);
  });
```

After:

```ts
  it('carries lucide\'s CANONICAL per-icon class over the WHOLE record vocabulary', () => {
    // ⚠️ RELAXED under the maintainer's ruling C on objectui#8941 (comment
    // 5750512894, verbatim 「8941 C」). This row USED TO REFUSE any seam glyph
    // whose complete class set differed from lucide's own component's. It NO
    // LONGER DOES, because lucide-react 1.43.0 emits one class per DECLARED
    // ALIAS (`house` renders `lucide-house lucide-home`) and no longer emits the
    // class it used to derive from the key, and the alias list exists only
    // inside each icon module — the modules objectui#9251 made lazy — while the
    // seam has to put its classes on the FIRST frame. The ruling chose the bump
    // over carrying every alias in the eager static name list (option A), and
    // it was taken knowing that it weakens this row. So a seam glyph missing
    // lucide's alias classes, or carrying the key-derived class lucide no longer
    // emits, now passes here.
    //
    // What it still refuses: a seam glyph without `lucide` or without lucide's
    // CANONICAL class, `lucide-ICONNAME`, which lucide emits first after the
    // bare `lucide`. That is the class a conversion rule gets wrong silently,
    // because many keys pack digits that lucide splits in the module name
    // (`ArrowDown01` is `lucide-arrow-down-0-1`, never `lucide-arrow-down01`).
    // Every name is still compared against the record's own component — not a
    // sample, and not a copy of the rule.
    const keys = Object.keys(icons);
    expect(keys.length).toBeGreaterThan(1000);
    const mismatches: string[] = [];
    let digitKeysChecked = 0;
    for (const key of keys) {
      if (/\d/.test(key)) digitKeysChecked += 1;
      const reference = renderIcon((icons as Record OF string, React.ElementType)[key], {});
      const seam = renderIcon(resolveIcon(key)!, {});
      // Read in lucide's own order: `lucide`, then the canonical class, then
      // one class per alias. Only the first two are required of the seam.
      const [base, canonical] = (reference?.getAttribute('class') ?? '').split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean);
      const got = classesOf(seam);
      if (base !== 'lucide' || !canonical?.startsWith('lucide-') || !got.includes(base) || !got.includes(canonical)) {
        mismatches.push(`${key}: expected "${base} ${canonical}" among "${got.join(' ')}"`);
      }
    }
    expect(mismatches.slice(0, 10)).toEqual([]);
    // Non-vacuity, both ways: the loop ran, and it ran over the class of name
    // this row exists for.
    expect(digitKeysChecked).toBeGreaterThan(50);
  });
```

### Pin 2 — `packages/components/src/renderers/form/__tests__/button-shared-icon-resolver.test.tsx`

Before (`6f20cfb06`):

```ts
    it('resolves `home` through the RENAME alias to House, not to a dead `home`', () => {
      // The single entry both maps carried. It is the one input whose answer
      // would have changed had the dedupe dropped the alias on the floor.
      const button = renderButton({ icon: 'home' });
      const house = button.querySelector('svg.lucide-house');
      expect(house).not.toBeNull();
      // The negative half used to read `querySelector('svg.lucide-home')` is
      // null. That form RETIRED on lucide-react 1.43.0, which reshaped
      // `createLucideIcon` to take an icon-data object carrying `aliases` and
      // to emit one class PER ALIAS: `house` now renders
      // `class="lucide lucide-house lucide-home ..."` itself, so the class no
      // longer says which glyph was drawn (measured: 248 of 1818 icon modules
      // carry aliases; 1.31.0 icon modules have no `aliases` field at all).
      // The discriminating form is below and still fires for the same defect:
      // `Home` is not a key of the runtime record, so had the rename been
      // dropped this button would render NO glyph at all, and any SECOND glyph
      // would be a different element from `house`.
      expect(button.querySelectorAll('svg')).toHaveLength(1);
      expect(button.querySelector('svg.lucide-home')).toBe(house);
    });
```

After:

```ts
    it('resolves `home` through the RENAME alias to House, not to a dead `home`', () => {
      // The single entry both maps carried. It is the one input whose answer
      // would have changed had the dedupe dropped the alias on the floor.
      const button = renderButton({ icon: 'home' });
      expect(button.querySelector('svg.lucide-house')).not.toBeNull();
      // ⚠️ RELAXED under the maintainer's ruling C on objectui#8941 (comment
      // 5750512894, verbatim 「8941 C」). This row USED TO REFUSE a house glyph
      // that did not also carry lucide's `lucide-home` ALIAS class on the same
      // element: `querySelector('svg.lucide-home')` had to BE the house svg. It
      // NO LONGER DOES, because this button draws through the objectui#9251
      // seam, which emits lucide's canonical class and not lucide-react
      // 1.43.0's per-alias classes, and the ruling accepted that rather than
      // put every icon's aliases into the eager static name list.
      //
      // ⛔ Nor does it go back to the older form, `svg.lucide-home` is null:
      // lucide 1.43.0 itself puts `lucide-home` on the house glyph, so that
      // class no longer says which glyph was drawn, and pinning its absence
      // would pin the seam's divergence from lucide. `lucide-home` is neither
      // required nor forbidden here. What still discriminates is the count:
      // `Home` is not a key of the runtime record, so had the rename been
      // dropped this button would render NO glyph at all.
      expect(button.querySelectorAll('svg')).toHaveLength(1);
    });
```

(On `main` this row still reads `expect(button.querySelector('svg.lucide-home')).toBeNull();`, which is green under the seam on either version. ⛔ It is not restored: lucide 1.43.0 puts `lucide-home` on the house glyph itself, so pinning its absence would pin the seam's divergence from lucide, and the row's own comment now says so.)

**Both relaxed rows can still fail, for what they still refuse.** Same tool and restore proof as 1d, each prediction written before its run:

```
PIN 1   mutation  return [fromKey, `lucide-${kebab}`, className]  ->  return [fromKey, className]
        RED       x carries lucide's CANONICAL per-icon class over the WHOLE record vocabulary
                  "ArrowDown01: expected \"lucide lucide-arrow-down-0-1\" among \"lucide lucide-arrow-down01\"" (and 9 more)
        restore   ok restored: blob == HEAD (99c47bc10373) and `git diff HEAD` is empty
PIN 2   mutation  delete the `Home: 'House',` rename entry
        RED       x resolves `home` through the RENAME alias to House    AssertionError: expected null not to be null
        restore   ok restored: blob == HEAD (99c47bc10373) and `git diff HEAD` is empty
```

(The first attempt at the pin-2 mutation passed an empty replacement, which the tool refuses; no test ran on it. The run above used its delete mode.)

**The seam's own docblock moved with the pins.** `lucideClassNames` claimed its classes were derived the way lucide derives them and that a pin caught either derivation drifting, under a test file name that does not exist. Neither survives this bump and this ruling, so it now says what the seam emits, what 1.43.0 emits instead, and which pin holds how much. Comment only; no code in `resolve-icon.ts` changed this round.

**⛔ No third pin.** The full suite ran locally at `989330df0` in 16 shards (`pnpm exec vitest run --shard=K/16`, each under `../objectstack/scripts/pm/os-verify-lock.sh`): **3618 test files** (3612 passed, 6 skipped, **0 failed**), **48571 tests** (48527 passed, 44 skipped, **0 failed**). CI on the same head: all eight `Test (shard N/8)` and `Test (dist pins)` green. No other pin went red, for this reason or for any other, so there was nothing to stop and report.

## 3. Checks

